1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,480
Once again, Haruhisa Kurabayashi joins the fray in the second half.

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:09,680
He seems to be adjusting very well to being on the first team.

3
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:16,640
There's something in his game that you might be able to incorporate into your own.

4
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,740
Whoa! He got the best crew!

5
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,820
There it is! This has to be what he meant!

6
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:31,820
Hmm? Hey, Aoi! You're not supposed to run in the hallway!

7
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:37,880
Coach Nozomi! Hey! Kurabayashi's game footage! I need everything!

8
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:16,786
Hey, what do you think you're doing? Pay attention, Aoi!

9
00:02:17,226 --> 00:02:19,846
Quit spacing out, dude. Wake up!

10
00:02:25,146 --> 00:02:28,446
What's your deal? You've been like a distracted zombie lately.

11
00:02:29,926 --> 00:02:31,006
Uh, sorry.

12
00:02:32,226 --> 00:02:35,846
You weren't even looking at the one who had the ball. Did you forget how to play?

13
00:02:35,986 --> 00:02:36,786
Course not.

14
00:02:37,366 --> 00:02:41,266
Seems like he's completely lost his motivation out there. What's going on?

15
00:02:42,826 --> 00:02:46,146
Haven't you noticed how unfocused and lazy he's been playing all week?

16
00:02:50,346 --> 00:02:56,526
You want to watch Kuribayashi play? Forget the killer pass. You should be watching footage of defenders instead.

17
00:02:56,526 --> 00:02:58,126
There's something I need to confirm first.

18
00:03:00,026 --> 00:03:02,966
It doesn't seem like a big deal, so I never thought about it.

19
00:03:03,786 --> 00:03:08,226
Even I was taught to do it when I was a kid. How special could it be?

20
00:03:09,226 --> 00:03:15,986
But I see it now. Kuribayashi goes to the extreme, doing it constantly all game long. It's a little freaky.

21
00:03:16,766 --> 00:03:22,086
Anyway, I would like to watch his past games. I want to see how long he's done it, and what for.

22
00:03:22,086 --> 00:03:26,166
Okay. Does this mean you're finally ready to play as a defender?

23
00:03:27,106 --> 00:03:31,526
I can't say I'm ready yet, but I'm gonna do it for them.

24
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:38,786
I don't want to cause any trouble for my teammates. I need to play at a strong enough level for them.

25
00:03:38,786 --> 00:03:41,586
I can't drag them down. No more!

26
00:03:47,166 --> 00:03:47,726
Owie!

27
00:03:48,606 --> 00:03:50,646
You were late with the shuffle again.

28
00:03:52,546 --> 00:03:53,526
Hey, Owie!

29
00:03:53,526 --> 00:04:01,386
Oh, jeez.

30
00:04:02,066 --> 00:04:04,566
That's a lot of head turns for a single match.

31
00:04:07,386 --> 00:04:08,826
Is he part chicken?

32
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:17,486
Right before he receives the ball, he turns his head left and right.

33
00:04:17,486 --> 00:04:22,886
Then after he receives it, he'll do it again.

34
00:04:23,446 --> 00:04:25,546
How does he not snap his damn neck?

35
00:04:26,286 --> 00:04:28,506
It looks like it takes him less than a second.

36
00:04:30,086 --> 00:04:32,106
He's doing it when the ball isn't near him.

37
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:34,226
It's all totally automatic.

38
00:04:35,046 --> 00:04:37,166
Turning my head like that would be a good skill.

39
00:04:37,566 --> 00:04:40,346
I'd know which players were around, and how many,

40
00:04:40,806 --> 00:04:42,626
which would tell me what needs to be done.

41
00:04:42,626 --> 00:04:44,986
Then I could plan my next move.

42
00:04:45,386 --> 00:04:48,026
These are different from the ones I learned when I was little.

43
00:04:48,366 --> 00:04:49,826
It won't be a simple adjustment.

44
00:04:50,326 --> 00:04:52,186
I'll have to learn his method from scratch.

45
00:04:56,066 --> 00:04:56,586
Idiot!

46
00:04:57,786 --> 00:05:01,786
In soccer, turning one's head is the most basic of the basics,

47
00:05:02,066 --> 00:05:04,886
but only a few can make full use of the technique.

48
00:05:05,526 --> 00:05:08,686
The rest just go through the motions without any strategic intention.

49
00:05:08,686 --> 00:05:12,926
A player should do it right before receiving the ball.

50
00:05:13,826 --> 00:05:17,686
Looking all around gives him a grasp on the state of the field in that moment.

51
00:05:19,386 --> 00:05:23,446
Also, it demonstrates to the other team that he is aware of his surroundings,

52
00:05:24,106 --> 00:05:25,866
discouraging them from tackling him,

53
00:05:26,266 --> 00:05:28,786
and making his teammates feel comfortable linking up.

54
00:05:29,486 --> 00:05:30,206
Listen to me.

55
00:05:30,566 --> 00:05:32,326
By watching Kuribayashi's game,

56
00:05:32,546 --> 00:05:34,906
you could find something to incorporate into your own.

57
00:05:34,906 --> 00:05:39,306
Good job, Ali.

58
00:05:39,566 --> 00:05:41,486
This is exactly what I was referring to.

59
00:05:41,666 --> 00:05:42,486
Just keep it up.

60
00:05:44,926 --> 00:05:46,826
This isn't working for me!

61
00:05:47,046 --> 00:05:49,486
I keep turning my head in all sorts of directions,

62
00:05:49,586 --> 00:05:51,006
and I don't know what I'm looking for!

63
00:05:51,386 --> 00:05:52,706
Screw being a fullback!

64
00:05:52,946 --> 00:05:55,806
I feel like I'm causing even more problems for my team now!

65
00:05:56,706 --> 00:05:57,186
Whoa!

66
00:05:57,386 --> 00:05:58,286
That's scary!

67
00:05:58,906 --> 00:06:00,146
Wait, wait, wait!

68
00:06:02,146 --> 00:06:02,386
Huh?

69
00:06:03,106 --> 00:06:03,626
Huh?

70
00:06:03,626 --> 00:06:06,726
I'm over this chicken dance for today.

71
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:09,086
It's a lot easier said than done.

72
00:06:09,806 --> 00:06:10,446
Ashito!

73
00:06:11,046 --> 00:06:11,966
Down the wing!

74
00:06:14,966 --> 00:06:15,446
Crap!

75
00:06:15,586 --> 00:06:16,886
I wasn't looking in front of me!

76
00:06:17,086 --> 00:06:17,686
Stay calm!

77
00:06:17,926 --> 00:06:19,426
I can just pass to Togashien!

78
00:06:19,426 --> 00:06:19,906
Huh?

79
00:06:30,906 --> 00:06:31,466
Right.

80
00:06:31,826 --> 00:06:33,366
Tell everyone to come in, Benson.

81
00:06:33,626 --> 00:06:37,526
I'm ready to announce the starters for the third match.

82
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:41,346
Man, it's been a while.

83
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:43,746
I wonder if everyone in the cafeteria missed me.

84
00:06:45,006 --> 00:06:46,566
Oh, there she is!

85
00:06:46,846 --> 00:06:47,486
Hi, Hana!

86
00:06:47,806 --> 00:06:50,246
This nice young man has been waiting to speak to you!

87
00:06:50,246 --> 00:07:05,386
I'm sure it's frustrating.

88
00:07:06,206 --> 00:07:06,726
Hey.

89
00:07:07,106 --> 00:07:07,386
Hi.

90
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,926
So I know these last games were rough,

91
00:07:10,106 --> 00:07:12,546
but after giving so much to the B team as a forward,

92
00:07:12,806 --> 00:07:16,066
it truly must be a gut punch not to even make the bench now.

93
00:07:16,066 --> 00:07:17,446
Oh, well.

94
00:07:17,446 --> 00:07:19,946
I've never played fullback.

95
00:07:20,366 --> 00:07:22,386
I can't just transform overnight.

96
00:07:22,386 --> 00:07:26,686
You don't seem as frustrated as I thought you'd be.

97
00:07:27,766 --> 00:07:28,946
I wanted to ask you.

98
00:07:29,126 --> 00:07:31,746
Before, when you told me to watch Kurabayashi's gameplay,

99
00:07:32,186 --> 00:07:34,246
was it about the head turns he does?

100
00:07:34,826 --> 00:07:35,266
Yes.

101
00:07:35,826 --> 00:07:38,326
Do you know of any drills to help learn that technique?

102
00:07:39,146 --> 00:07:40,306
Like, how do I master?

103
00:07:40,306 --> 00:07:45,906
I mean, it's a lot to be aware of.

104
00:07:46,146 --> 00:07:48,086
I want to be able to do it unconsciously.

105
00:07:48,366 --> 00:07:48,866
Like him.

106
00:07:52,566 --> 00:07:53,266
This is it!

107
00:07:53,486 --> 00:07:54,366
This is a test!

108
00:07:54,666 --> 00:07:55,646
I want to be a manager!

109
00:07:55,966 --> 00:07:58,066
This is my chance to show off what I can do!

110
00:07:59,806 --> 00:08:00,926
So you...

111
00:08:00,926 --> 00:08:02,086
you made this meal plan?

112
00:08:02,946 --> 00:08:03,306
Dang.

113
00:08:03,786 --> 00:08:05,866
I had a feeling I was missing a page on this one.

114
00:08:06,526 --> 00:08:07,446
It's quite impressive.

115
00:08:07,446 --> 00:08:10,126
The lunch lady told me you were the one who laid it out.

116
00:08:10,646 --> 00:08:12,326
She worked really hard on it

117
00:08:12,326 --> 00:08:14,686
and even consulted our menu for healthy options.

118
00:08:15,046 --> 00:08:16,206
All for a player she liked.

119
00:08:16,406 --> 00:08:18,066
Well, that's so sweet!

120
00:08:20,146 --> 00:08:23,426
I didn't expect something like this out of Manager Fukuda's sister.

121
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:26,306
You would come by to help all the time

122
00:08:26,306 --> 00:08:28,126
when we were on the junior youth team together.

123
00:08:28,386 --> 00:08:29,506
Wow! So cool!

124
00:08:29,706 --> 00:08:32,766
The great Kurabayashi, a world-renowned player, knows who I am!

125
00:08:32,766 --> 00:08:36,826
You used to patch me up when I was injured.

126
00:08:37,466 --> 00:08:38,006
So yeah.

127
00:08:40,006 --> 00:08:40,606
Whoa!

128
00:08:41,726 --> 00:08:44,226
I thought that might be you, Kurabayashi!

129
00:08:44,906 --> 00:08:47,426
Asperion's shining star and our great hope!

130
00:08:47,726 --> 00:08:48,786
Um, thank you.

131
00:08:49,326 --> 00:08:51,626
We'll be counting on you in the next game!

132
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:52,646
Love you!

133
00:08:53,706 --> 00:08:54,226
Later!

134
00:08:54,226 --> 00:08:59,746
Everybody loves you!

135
00:09:00,106 --> 00:09:01,866
Guess that happens when you're world famous-

136
00:09:01,866 --> 00:09:02,906
I want to be the best.

137
00:09:04,646 --> 00:09:05,846
In the whole world.

138
00:09:07,846 --> 00:09:09,446
Do you think you could help me?

139
00:09:11,326 --> 00:09:11,766
There.

140
00:09:12,006 --> 00:09:13,486
I need a meal plan just like that.

141
00:09:13,706 --> 00:09:14,126
For real.

142
00:09:15,246 --> 00:09:16,606
But I'm a picky eater.

143
00:09:16,906 --> 00:09:18,346
I refuse to eat peppers.

144
00:09:18,546 --> 00:09:19,186
Or carrots.

145
00:09:19,426 --> 00:09:20,486
What? Are you a child?

146
00:09:21,266 --> 00:09:22,806
Still, you're joking, right?

147
00:09:22,806 --> 00:09:25,766
I mean, it's not like high-end or anything.

148
00:09:26,206 --> 00:09:27,906
You put so much work into it.

149
00:09:28,206 --> 00:09:30,226
I'm assuming that's what you want to do for a career.

150
00:09:31,046 --> 00:09:32,346
Sports nutrition, I mean.

151
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,466
I play in a professional league, you know.

152
00:09:36,426 --> 00:09:38,726
I would be a walking billboard for new clients.

153
00:09:39,126 --> 00:09:40,046
Just think about it.

154
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:53,666
Okay, fine.

155
00:09:54,046 --> 00:09:54,866
On one condition.

156
00:09:55,726 --> 00:09:56,406
What's that?

157
00:09:57,486 --> 00:10:01,146
Well, um, my friend Ashita wants to play like you someday.

158
00:10:01,866 --> 00:10:04,246
Could you maybe give him some point-

159
00:10:04,246 --> 00:10:04,646
Uh-huh.

160
00:10:15,646 --> 00:10:16,006
What?

161
00:10:20,546 --> 00:10:20,906
Nothing.

162
00:10:21,266 --> 00:10:22,266
I'll get started on it.

163
00:10:23,366 --> 00:10:23,726
Hmm?

164
00:10:23,726 --> 00:10:29,246
You have to find a way to make turning your head a habit, Aoi.

165
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:32,726
Consciously incorporate it into your daily training.

166
00:10:33,746 --> 00:10:33,906
Hmm?

167
00:10:34,486 --> 00:10:34,926
Huh?

168
00:10:35,606 --> 00:10:36,846
Start with ball juggling.

169
00:10:37,446 --> 00:10:37,846
Oh.

170
00:10:39,006 --> 00:10:41,646
Then, do a kick, and while it's high in the air,

171
00:10:41,966 --> 00:10:44,626
look left and right, and catch it.

172
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,866
Also, don't just turn your head.

173
00:10:47,186 --> 00:10:50,046
Try to spot something and make a note of it as you look each way.

174
00:10:50,046 --> 00:10:53,946
For example, a pebble, a leaf.

175
00:10:54,306 --> 00:10:57,006
I catch it on my foot, and then I repeat it.

176
00:10:57,486 --> 00:10:57,626
Huh?

177
00:10:58,126 --> 00:10:58,626
I-

178
00:10:58,626 --> 00:11:00,606
Um, it's pretty basic.

179
00:11:00,866 --> 00:11:01,826
Sure, you already know.

180
00:11:02,846 --> 00:11:04,506
Your ball control's awesome.

181
00:11:05,226 --> 00:11:06,846
Wow, you really think so?

182
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:08,586
Yeah, and you're right.

183
00:11:08,706 --> 00:11:09,666
I do know that drill.

184
00:11:10,406 --> 00:11:10,626
Huh?

185
00:11:11,286 --> 00:11:12,586
Oh, I'm sorry.

186
00:11:13,166 --> 00:11:15,486
But, I never knew I was supposed to spot things.

187
00:11:15,566 --> 00:11:16,306
That makes sense.

188
00:11:16,686 --> 00:11:17,366
I'll do it.

189
00:11:17,586 --> 00:11:19,066
At least a thousand times.

190
00:11:19,066 --> 00:11:21,386
I'll have it down by the next match.

191
00:11:24,986 --> 00:11:26,966
He's being so positive about it.

192
00:11:27,226 --> 00:11:28,846
They made him change his position,

193
00:11:29,186 --> 00:11:31,366
and then didn't even put him on the bench for the game.

194
00:11:31,606 --> 00:11:32,886
But instead of sulking,

195
00:11:33,286 --> 00:11:35,266
he's taking the time to work on his skills.

196
00:11:35,826 --> 00:11:37,086
It hasn't even been a week

197
00:11:37,086 --> 00:11:39,266
since I saw his face looking so lost.

198
00:11:43,646 --> 00:11:44,786
He's so cute.

199
00:11:44,786 --> 00:11:51,346
That pass I made to Otomo earlier.

200
00:11:51,346 --> 00:11:54,666
I did it unconsciously.

201
00:11:55,026 --> 00:11:57,426
I have no idea how I did that.

202
00:11:57,426 --> 00:12:01,566
The only thing I changed was turning my head.

203
00:12:01,966 --> 00:12:03,606
I wasn't looking at anything specific,

204
00:12:04,086 --> 00:12:05,206
but something happened.

205
00:12:05,606 --> 00:12:06,946
For a split second.

206
00:12:07,506 --> 00:12:09,106
What exactly was that?

207
00:12:09,426 --> 00:12:11,046
I feel like it's happened before.

208
00:12:11,546 --> 00:12:13,626
It was super quick, but I remember it.

209
00:12:13,626 --> 00:12:15,646
I saw it very clearly.

210
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:18,706
Up until then, it was in the corner of my mind.

211
00:12:19,266 --> 00:12:21,526
It resembled a bunch of ants swarming around.

212
00:12:22,286 --> 00:12:24,746
Suddenly, I was able to connect to that vision.

213
00:12:25,246 --> 00:12:27,746
I don't think there are words to truly describe it.

214
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:30,046
But who cares?

215
00:12:30,366 --> 00:12:31,006
It happened.

216
00:12:31,486 --> 00:12:33,726
I turned my head, and something changed.

217
00:12:33,966 --> 00:12:35,826
So I'll stay out and practice

218
00:12:35,826 --> 00:12:37,726
until I'm just as good as Kurabayashi.

219
00:12:38,086 --> 00:12:41,046
I might be about to grasp onto something great.

220
00:12:41,646 --> 00:12:42,186
For real.

221
00:12:42,666 --> 00:12:44,086
Your vision's really wide.

222
00:12:47,086 --> 00:12:47,646
Vision.

223
00:12:47,646 --> 00:12:47,766
Vision.

224
00:12:57,746 --> 00:13:13,686
The situation's critical.

225
00:13:14,626 --> 00:13:16,726
We've lost four games in a row.

226
00:13:17,186 --> 00:13:17,926
You see this?

227
00:13:18,166 --> 00:13:19,286
This is our team.

228
00:13:19,786 --> 00:13:21,606
Right there in the relegation zone.

229
00:13:22,526 --> 00:13:24,446
Even the second tier team plays

230
00:13:24,446 --> 00:13:26,146
at Tokyo Metropolis League level.

231
00:13:26,146 --> 00:13:29,086
That's the strength of Asperion youth.

232
00:13:30,266 --> 00:13:31,926
And if we are relegated,

233
00:13:32,106 --> 00:13:33,926
it limits our team's potential next year

234
00:13:33,926 --> 00:13:34,966
and for years after.

235
00:13:35,226 --> 00:13:36,146
I agree with you.

236
00:13:36,446 --> 00:13:38,366
We have worked too hard to lose it all now.

237
00:13:38,706 --> 00:13:41,446
Not getting demoted is the least I expect of B team.

238
00:13:42,046 --> 00:13:43,946
I may have moved up to A team,

239
00:13:43,946 --> 00:13:46,646
but I'm still pulling for everyone on B team to succeed.

240
00:13:47,466 --> 00:13:49,646
I know what you're capable of.

241
00:13:50,126 --> 00:13:51,146
I'm sorry, you guys.

242
00:13:52,046 --> 00:13:53,586
It's not just Tachibana.

243
00:13:54,046 --> 00:13:56,026
The forwards in general aren't scoring enough.

244
00:13:56,706 --> 00:13:59,946
The defenders aren't doing so hot either.

245
00:14:00,306 --> 00:14:02,606
We've let way too many goals get through lately.

246
00:14:02,926 --> 00:14:03,626
Ask Togashi.

247
00:14:04,246 --> 00:14:05,786
He's so committed to ignoring me

248
00:14:05,786 --> 00:14:07,146
that he won't even make eye contact.

249
00:14:07,546 --> 00:14:08,866
And we're both defenders.

250
00:14:10,306 --> 00:14:11,506
I've let you down.

251
00:14:11,786 --> 00:14:12,266
I'm sorry.

252
00:14:12,266 --> 00:14:15,426
I haven't scored any goals at all.

253
00:14:16,426 --> 00:14:18,646
There's plenty of blame to go around, Tachibana,

254
00:14:18,726 --> 00:14:20,026
so don't take it all on yourself.

255
00:14:20,426 --> 00:14:21,526
Gotta ease up, man.

256
00:14:22,086 --> 00:14:23,086
Hey, be real.

257
00:14:23,566 --> 00:14:24,366
What's with Coach?

258
00:14:24,546 --> 00:14:26,566
Do you think he's bringing Aoi back as a forward?

259
00:14:26,566 --> 00:14:31,206
Oh, that reminds me.

260
00:14:31,426 --> 00:14:32,906
Ashito isn't here yet, is he?

261
00:14:33,026 --> 00:14:33,826
Is he running late?

262
00:14:33,986 --> 00:14:36,326
I really hope he wouldn't miss such an important meeting.

263
00:14:36,466 --> 00:14:37,366
You know what I mean?

264
00:14:37,866 --> 00:14:39,166
Aoi stayed back as usual.

265
00:14:39,706 --> 00:14:40,786
He wanted to keep practicing.

266
00:14:40,786 --> 00:14:44,086
You haven't noticed?

267
00:14:44,406 --> 00:14:46,466
He trains for an hour or so after we get out.

268
00:14:46,706 --> 00:14:48,726
He's done it every day for the past month, at least.

269
00:14:49,826 --> 00:14:51,906
We don't have time to talk about players

270
00:14:51,906 --> 00:14:53,006
who aren't even on the bench.

271
00:14:53,326 --> 00:14:55,146
We gotta focus on the actual team.

272
00:14:55,926 --> 00:14:57,186
Offense, let's focus.

273
00:14:57,486 --> 00:14:58,366
We're out of time.

274
00:14:58,926 --> 00:15:01,446
Cause soon, we play the top team on this board.

275
00:15:02,006 --> 00:15:03,326
It's time to step it up.

276
00:15:05,486 --> 00:15:06,986
That can't be.

277
00:15:07,466 --> 00:15:08,486
Are these stats real?

278
00:15:09,346 --> 00:15:12,406
Six wins, zero losses, and a goal difference of 17?

279
00:15:12,966 --> 00:15:14,086
Were they always this strong?

280
00:15:16,086 --> 00:15:17,826
I don't know anything for sure,

281
00:15:18,006 --> 00:15:19,926
but I heard they got a new manager this year.

282
00:15:20,466 --> 00:15:23,106
One of their high-ranking junior youth coaches got promoted.

283
00:15:23,386 --> 00:15:24,266
So, yeah.

284
00:15:24,266 --> 00:15:26,666
Regardless, their strength's extraordinary.

285
00:15:27,466 --> 00:15:29,246
They're the last team we want to face,

286
00:15:29,466 --> 00:15:31,526
especially in the state we're in right now.

287
00:15:33,746 --> 00:15:35,146
Wait a sec, Tachibana.

288
00:15:35,586 --> 00:15:37,146
Didn't you used to play for Musashino?

289
00:15:46,386 --> 00:15:48,406
You're still out here practicing this late?

290
00:15:49,806 --> 00:15:51,046
Hey there, Tachibana.

291
00:15:51,206 --> 00:15:51,886
Aw, crap!

292
00:15:52,026 --> 00:15:53,146
Did I miss the team meeting?

293
00:15:54,266 --> 00:15:55,146
I'm so sorry.

294
00:15:55,466 --> 00:15:57,406
I figured since I'm not even on the bench,

295
00:15:57,466 --> 00:15:58,906
I didn't have much to contribute anyway.

296
00:15:59,106 --> 00:16:01,126
So I decided to prioritize practicing.

297
00:16:01,506 --> 00:16:02,726
I'll just be a little longer.

298
00:16:03,366 --> 00:16:05,206
You can head back to the dorm without me.

299
00:16:06,146 --> 00:16:08,366
You know, I think you're amazing.

300
00:16:08,906 --> 00:16:09,546
I am?

301
00:16:09,546 --> 00:16:11,146
You don't sulk.

302
00:16:11,606 --> 00:16:12,206
Like ever.

303
00:16:13,006 --> 00:16:15,026
I don't know anyone who works harder than you.

304
00:16:15,566 --> 00:16:16,406
Is that so?

305
00:16:16,746 --> 00:16:17,246
It is.

306
00:16:17,566 --> 00:16:18,886
Even when you're not on the field,

307
00:16:18,966 --> 00:16:20,686
you pay close attention to every game

308
00:16:20,686 --> 00:16:21,926
and cheer us all on.

309
00:16:22,326 --> 00:16:23,346
Okay, stop.

310
00:16:24,206 --> 00:16:26,046
I was with you up until the cheering part,

311
00:16:26,186 --> 00:16:27,786
but I am working on ways to help.

312
00:16:28,346 --> 00:16:28,606
Huh?

313
00:16:28,966 --> 00:16:30,606
All that stuff's new, by the way.

314
00:16:31,606 --> 00:16:31,966
Really?

315
00:16:32,126 --> 00:16:33,646
I used to be the king of Solking.

316
00:16:34,046 --> 00:16:36,286
I would refuse to watch any game I didn't play in.

317
00:16:36,606 --> 00:16:38,346
I mean, that's super frustrating, you know?

318
00:16:39,306 --> 00:16:40,546
But this past month,

319
00:16:40,626 --> 00:16:43,306
I really started to think seriously about my vision.

320
00:16:43,566 --> 00:16:44,926
And I'm actually learning a lot

321
00:16:44,926 --> 00:16:46,366
just by sitting on the sidelines.

322
00:16:47,526 --> 00:16:47,966
Tons!

323
00:16:47,966 --> 00:16:52,606
I watch and think about what I would do in that position.

324
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:55,086
Like, I'll notice how a guy didn't look toward the middle

325
00:16:55,086 --> 00:16:57,166
and ask what would have happened if he did.

326
00:16:57,406 --> 00:16:59,346
I work out scenarios like little puzzles

327
00:16:59,346 --> 00:17:00,546
as I observe the game.

328
00:17:00,866 --> 00:17:02,246
It makes the time fly by.

329
00:17:02,706 --> 00:17:04,406
So I'm not the perfect cheerleader.

330
00:17:05,766 --> 00:17:06,206
Sorry.

331
00:17:08,766 --> 00:17:10,966
Can you teach me how to be just like you?

332
00:17:10,966 --> 00:17:11,566
Hmm?

333
00:17:17,966 --> 00:17:18,406
Hmm.

334
00:17:19,586 --> 00:17:20,226
Hey!

335
00:17:20,546 --> 00:17:21,226
Tachibana!

336
00:17:21,646 --> 00:17:22,186
Ashito!

337
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:24,386
We need to eat our feelings!

338
00:17:24,726 --> 00:17:25,406
You want to join?

339
00:17:25,686 --> 00:17:26,886
How about Okonomiyaki?

340
00:17:27,286 --> 00:17:28,526
Yeah, sounds good!

341
00:17:28,806 --> 00:17:30,026
You're in, right, Tachibana?

342
00:17:32,946 --> 00:17:35,086
So, which place are we going to?

343
00:17:35,946 --> 00:17:36,826
Let's see.

344
00:17:37,046 --> 00:17:37,946
It is close.

345
00:17:38,326 --> 00:17:39,666
Mustachino's number one.

346
00:17:43,866 --> 00:17:46,366
The game against Asperion youth is coming up.

347
00:17:46,366 --> 00:17:50,586
I can't wait to see Tachibana and Otomo and Aoi.

348
00:17:53,326 --> 00:17:55,106
I wonder how much they've improved.

349
00:17:59,406 --> 00:18:01,326
What do you mean you don't want to go to Musashino?

350
00:18:01,726 --> 00:18:03,206
Isn't that your hometown, Tachibana?

351
00:18:03,686 --> 00:18:04,726
What's your damage, bro?

352
00:18:05,166 --> 00:18:06,186
It is my hometown.

353
00:18:06,886 --> 00:18:08,186
That's why I don't want to go.

354
00:18:08,466 --> 00:18:10,506
Please don't do this to me, Tachibana!

355
00:18:10,606 --> 00:18:13,366
My mind's in a full-blown Okonomiyaki mode right now

356
00:18:13,366 --> 00:18:15,106
and I can't eat anywhere else!

357
00:18:15,106 --> 00:18:19,106
Until I start contributing to Asperion,

358
00:18:19,586 --> 00:18:21,546
I'd rather not return home at disappointment.

359
00:18:22,066 --> 00:18:23,706
I don't believe any of that, Bull.

360
00:18:24,066 --> 00:18:26,806
You're always going home whenever we have some time off.

361
00:18:27,166 --> 00:18:27,486
Really?

362
00:18:27,806 --> 00:18:29,526
I visit my grandfather in Sugamo.

363
00:18:30,126 --> 00:18:31,986
He lives alone, so I check up on him.

364
00:18:32,126 --> 00:18:33,106
Aw, you angel.

365
00:18:33,106 --> 00:18:36,706
Anyway, I'm keeping that promise to myself.

366
00:18:36,706 --> 00:18:39,766
You know, I feel you on not wanting to go home

367
00:18:39,766 --> 00:18:41,706
until you can show him you've accomplished something.

368
00:18:41,866 --> 00:18:43,366
But we're just going to eat.

369
00:18:43,626 --> 00:18:44,446
Enough talking!

370
00:18:44,446 --> 00:18:50,746
You know, Tachibana, you can be a little dramatic at times.

371
00:18:50,886 --> 00:18:51,446
Just saying.

372
00:18:52,226 --> 00:18:54,126
Stop taking matches so personal.

373
00:18:54,386 --> 00:18:57,266
Like when we're losing pretty big, you get all depressed, bro.

374
00:18:57,646 --> 00:18:58,546
It's just a game.

375
00:18:58,726 --> 00:19:00,066
It's not that huge a deal.

376
00:19:00,326 --> 00:19:01,926
Because our team hasn't been scoring.

377
00:19:01,926 --> 00:19:04,866
And as a forward, that makes me feel responsible.

378
00:19:05,106 --> 00:19:06,006
You lost me!

379
00:19:06,326 --> 00:19:08,626
I don't give two craps long as I'm playing well.

380
00:19:08,786 --> 00:19:10,926
Because I know if we lose, it's not my fault.

381
00:19:11,026 --> 00:19:11,806
It's someone else's.

382
00:19:11,886 --> 00:19:14,746
Now, if we win, that's 100% my fault.

383
00:19:14,866 --> 00:19:15,666
It's that easy.

384
00:19:16,206 --> 00:19:18,266
I get super nervous right before a match.

385
00:19:18,526 --> 00:19:20,266
Once it's over, though, that's it for me.

386
00:19:20,686 --> 00:19:22,666
It's in the past, and that's where it stays.

387
00:19:22,886 --> 00:19:23,726
Gotta move on.

388
00:19:25,466 --> 00:19:26,366
How about you?

389
00:19:26,366 --> 00:19:28,106
I don't know.

390
00:19:28,946 --> 00:19:30,546
I don't really play much these days.

391
00:19:30,686 --> 00:19:31,406
It doesn't matter.

392
00:19:32,806 --> 00:19:34,866
Honestly, I get how you feel, Tachibana.

393
00:19:36,226 --> 00:19:37,726
This is the way I see it.

394
00:19:38,086 --> 00:19:41,626
Anytime I play in a game, I'm responsible for the moves I make.

395
00:19:42,406 --> 00:19:46,026
Let me put it a different way.

396
00:19:46,186 --> 00:19:48,026
It's my fault if we win or lose.

397
00:19:48,146 --> 00:19:50,406
And that makes me the most powerful player on the team.

398
00:19:50,786 --> 00:19:51,926
What are you saying?

399
00:19:52,106 --> 00:19:53,126
So, like, when we lose,

400
00:19:53,126 --> 00:19:56,206
I start thinking about how to help the team win the next game.

401
00:19:56,366 --> 00:19:58,466
I get so excited for the next match

402
00:19:58,466 --> 00:20:00,426
that I start practicing for it right then.

403
00:20:00,726 --> 00:20:03,166
You are the wind beneath our wings, Ashito.

404
00:20:10,986 --> 00:20:11,746
Let me see.

405
00:20:11,846 --> 00:20:13,646
You're supposed to be right by the train station.

406
00:20:14,486 --> 00:20:15,006
Tachibana!

407
00:20:15,246 --> 00:20:17,046
You want to help since this is your town?

408
00:20:19,606 --> 00:20:21,026
Oh, my gosh!

409
00:20:21,026 --> 00:20:27,746
No way!

410
00:20:27,846 --> 00:20:28,886
It's Nakano!

411
00:20:29,186 --> 00:20:30,026
Is that Aoi?

412
00:20:30,226 --> 00:20:30,966
And Tachibana?

413
00:20:31,306 --> 00:20:31,866
And Ultimo?

414
00:20:32,686 --> 00:20:33,126
Nakano!

415
00:20:33,826 --> 00:20:35,146
I can't believe it!

416
00:20:36,006 --> 00:20:36,946
It's been forever!

417
00:20:36,946 --> 00:20:37,426
I knew it!

418
00:20:37,626 --> 00:20:39,206
One glance and I just knew it!

419
00:20:39,566 --> 00:20:40,866
Are we going to eat or not?

420
00:20:40,966 --> 00:20:41,886
Who's this guy?

421
00:20:42,126 --> 00:20:42,886
It's Nakano!

422
00:20:43,346 --> 00:20:46,726
He was our brother in arms back during the Asperion tryouts!

423
00:20:46,726 --> 00:20:50,146
Anyway, how you been, man?

424
00:20:51,406 --> 00:20:54,126
So he's one of the losers that didn't make it.

425
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:56,546
They consider him a brother in arms.

426
00:20:56,626 --> 00:20:56,946
Seriously!

427
00:20:58,206 --> 00:20:59,246
But that's it!

428
00:20:59,546 --> 00:21:01,486
His round eyes haven't changed one bit!

429
00:21:02,826 --> 00:21:03,846
They're very cute.

430
00:21:05,226 --> 00:21:06,586
Hey, Nakano.

431
00:21:06,926 --> 00:21:07,526
That kid.

432
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,746
I don't understand.

433
00:21:08,746 --> 00:21:13,086
Oh, yeah.

434
00:21:13,666 --> 00:21:14,446
About that.

435
00:21:14,826 --> 00:21:17,206
I played for Tokyo Musashino's youth team.

436
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:17,866
Huh?

437
00:21:18,306 --> 00:21:19,346
Tachibana's old team?

438
00:21:19,526 --> 00:21:20,566
What the heck do you mean?

439
00:21:21,386 --> 00:21:24,586
After failing in the tryouts, I was scouted.

440
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:26,906
Manager Satake recruited me.

441
00:21:27,146 --> 00:21:28,326
That's who's coaching us now.

442
00:21:31,766 --> 00:21:33,086
Obviously, we both accepted.

443
00:21:33,386 --> 00:21:34,666
We would have been crazy not to.

444
00:21:35,026 --> 00:21:35,746
You both?

445
00:21:36,266 --> 00:21:36,706
Nakano.

446
00:21:36,706 --> 00:21:37,306
Huh?

447
00:21:38,746 --> 00:21:43,706
What?

448
00:21:43,926 --> 00:21:44,326
Kaneda?

449
00:21:44,766 --> 00:21:45,466
No way!

450
00:21:45,546 --> 00:21:46,686
You've got to be kidding me!

451
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:48,806
You're playing on the same team as Nakano now?

452
00:21:48,986 --> 00:21:49,846
That's amazing!

453
00:21:50,366 --> 00:21:52,106
We can all go to dinner and catch up.

454
00:21:52,346 --> 00:21:53,486
Whoa, look at you.

455
00:21:53,666 --> 00:21:55,306
You've blown up at least one size.

456
00:21:56,246 --> 00:21:56,426
Huh?

457
00:21:56,866 --> 00:21:58,306
Get your hands off me!

458
00:21:58,306 --> 00:21:58,766
Huh?

459
00:22:04,766 --> 00:22:06,166
It makes no sense.

460
00:22:06,166 --> 00:22:08,786
I never expected you to get past the first round.

461
00:22:11,126 --> 00:22:13,126
During those stupid tryouts.

462
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:17,766
I couldn't focus because of you guys.

463
00:22:18,646 --> 00:22:19,766
You ruined it.

464
00:22:21,126 --> 00:22:24,066
And for that, I will never forgive you!

465
00:22:24,066 --> 00:22:25,606
チャー chains are nailed.

466
00:22:27,066 --> 00:22:28,066
Why does stupid tryouts?

467
00:22:29,246 --> 00:22:29,366
I don't care what happens.

468
00:22:31,826 --> 00:22:32,346
You're not right.

469
00:22:32,426 --> 00:22:33,546
I do not know.

470
00:22:34,006 --> 00:22:34,206
I will never forgive you.

471
00:22:34,206 --> 00:22:34,546
I will never forgive you, man.

472
00:22:34,966 --> 00:22:35,306
сбasaki out.

473
00:22:36,706 --> 00:22:37,126
I will never be right away.

474
00:22:37,286 --> 00:22:37,866
You're late.

475
00:22:38,066 --> 00:22:38,586
I will never be right away.

476
00:22:42,666 --> 00:22:43,406
I will never forget you.

477
00:22:43,666 --> 00:22:44,966
zwischen you once said...

478
00:22:47,846 --> 00:22:48,526
Excuse me, kau Anti-

479
00:22:48,546 --> 00:22:49,106
ency, you're welcome.

480
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:49,846
You're right.

481
00:22:49,926 --> 00:22:50,746
Not ma'aları, I will never forget you.

